CONCLUSION
\par
Recognizing the importance of being environmen-
\par
tally sustainable, this study has offered insight to firms
\par
to achieve environmental management capabilities in
\par
terms of corporate environmental innovativeness and
\par
adaptability. While prior studies are confined to spe-
\par
cific environmental management practices, for exam-
\par
ple, eco-product development and sustainable supply
\par
management (Paulraj, 2011; Russo \& Harrison,
\par
2005), and their impact on organizational perfor-
\par
mance, this study considers corporate environmental
\par
innovativeness and adaptability as organizational
\par
capabilities of environmental management to achieve
\par
financial and environmental performance. Based on
\par
DC theory, the findings extend prior research by sug-
\par
gesting that corporate environmental innovativeness
\par
and adaptability are valuable to firms in achieving
\par
their environmental objectives, as well as improving
\par
financial performance.
\par
Furthermore, this study revealed that EII facilitates
\par
information sharing across internal and external busi-
\par
ness processes, enabling collaboration across functions
\par
and supply chain partners. Acknowledging the differ-
\par
ences of different dimensions of integration in supply
\par
chain management (Wong et al., 2011c), this study
\par
reveals the value of internal, customer and supplier
\par
EII in contributing to environmental management
\par
capabilities. Although supplier EII is found to be
\par
insufficient in enabling corporate environmental
\par
innovativeness and adaptability, the finding suggests
\par
the importance of customer EII in providing valuable
\par
information related to environmental expectations and
\par
requirements. The study also suggests that internal EII
\par
is useful for firms to orchestrate business processes and
\par
respond to new environmental requirements. Firms
\par
should therefore make deliberate efforts to establish
\par
internal EII and collaborate with customers to share
\par
environmental information, to facilitate environmental
\par
sustainability in their operations.
