Entropy Score in Boolean Networks
\par
Boolean networks were first introduced by Somogyi
\par
and Sniegoski.33 Liang et al.34 introduced a search
\par
algorithm in Boolean networks called REVEAL
\par
(REVerse Engineering ALgorithm).
\par
REVEAL uses mutual information among nodes
\par
in search of a structure. Liang et al.34 defined entropy
\par
of a gene Xi as H(Xi)= -p0 log p0- p1 log p1, where
\par
p0 and p1 are the maximum likelihood of 0s
\par
and 1s (as an expression level of the gene Xi)
\par
from data respectively. Also defined is H(Xi, Xj)=
\par
- k,l{$\in$}\textbraceleft 0,1\textbraceright{} pkl log pkl, where pkl represents the max-
\par
imum likelihood estimate from the data of the joint
\par
expression level of Xi as k and Xj as l. Finally, mutual
\par
information is defined as follows:
\par
M(Xi, Xj)= H(Xj)- H(Xj\textbar Xi)= H(Xi)- H(Xi\textbar Xj),
\par
where H(Xi \textbar{} Xj)= H(Xi, Xj)- H(Xj) and H(Xj \textbar{}
\par
Xi)= H(Xi, Xj)- H(Xi). Using mutual information
\par
their search algorithm has three stages: (1) search for
\par
all pairs Xi and Xj1 and check whether M(Xi, Xj1)=
\par
H(Xi). Whenever the condition is satisfied, a Boolean
\par
function is assigned between Xi and Xj1, i.e. Xj1 deter-
\par
mines Xi; (2) if there is any Xiwith no function assign-
\par
ment, then test whether M(Xi, Xj1, Xj2)= H(Xi) for
\par
all Xj1, Xj2; (3) repeat the second stage by adding addi-
\par
tional Xj to the previous condition. In the worst case,
\par
the search algorithm will check the condition M(Xi,
\par
Xj1, Xj2,. . . , Xjn-1)= H(Xi), where n is the number
\par
of modeled genes. Akutsu et al.35 gave a mathematical
\par
proof of the observation of Liang et al.34 that a small
\par
number of state transition (INPUT/OUTPUT) pairs
\par
are sufficient in order to infer the original Boolean
\par
network. More systems that use Boolean networks
\par
were introduced with some added functions.36--38
\par
With its simple representation, Boolean net-
\par
works were easily implemented as genetic networks.
\par
However, since Boolean networks do not explicitly
\par
model uncertainty, they cannot model the stochastic
\par
behavior of a biological system.
\par
