\par
\dh 16\TH{}
\par
and are used to swap genes with the corresponding ones of the
\par
other parent. The crossover operation is often considered to find
\par
local optima. An offspring will be also generated by a mutation
\par
operation to jump out the current local optima. In the mutation
\par
operation, a chromosome is selected with probability 0.08, and
\par
then some genes (cp and C) of the chromosome are mutated to
\par
generate an offspring. The genes for mutation points are randomly
\par
selected (Koza and Poli, 2005) with probability 0.5. A mutation
\par
operation aims at producing new offspring chromosomes to jump
\par
out current local optima.
\par
The fitness of individuals is NPm as a function of cp and C. The
\par
production capacity violation given by constraint (7) is not consid-
\par
