5. Numerical examples
\par
It is intuitively understandable that the retailer selection strat-
\par
egy leads to higher performance than the non-selection strategy.
\par
To explicitly demonstrate the impacts of retailer selection based
\par
on the proposed Stackelberg game model and the hybrid algorithm
\par
on both the manufacturer and retailers' profits, we carry out
\par
numerical examples for two strategies: retailer selection and
\par
non-selection, and compare their results. We further validate the
\par
above impacts by conducting sensitivity analyses. These sensitivity
\par
analyses are also used to explain the reasons for retailers being se-
\par
lected or rejected. We also carry out numerical studies to evaluate
\par
the performance of the proposed hybrid algorithm.
\par
In the numerical examples, the hybrid algorithm is coded in
\par
Matlab 2010a on a Core 2 Duo 3.0 GHz CPU and 3 G RAM. In the
\par
DP algorithm, we set the granularity of P discretization as 20.
\par
