2.2 The COPD Model
\par
We created a discrete time Markov model of COPD to
\par
estimate costs, exacerbation rates, and quality-adjusted
\par
life-years (QALYs) for each treatment. Costs were reported
\par
in year 2011 Canadian dollars (\$).The outputs of the model
\par
were the discounted 10-year costs, number of exacerba-
\par
tions, and QALYs associated with each treatment. A
\par
schematic illustration of the model is provided in Fig. 2.
\par
The model structure is similar to the widely used Burden of
\par
Obstructive Lung Disease (BOLD) COPD model [13].
\par
COPD stages were classified as mild (stage I), moderate
\par
(stage II), and severe (stage III) according to the Global
\par
Initiative for Obstructive Lung Disease (GOLD) criteria
\par
[14]. The target population for this study was patients with
\par
moderate-to-severe COPD (stages II and III), as studies
\par
