\par
EVPPIs, adjusted for time and population horizon of the
\par
decision context, sets an upper limit for the benefit of
\par
future studies that will generate evidence for the decision
\par
task [3]. In this work, we focused on individual EVPI and
\par
EVPPI, as converting them from individual level to pop-
\par
ulation level is independent of the way the evidence on the
\par
effect size is generated, and would have no effect on the
\par
overall interpretation of our findings.
\par
A future RCT might not necessarily incorporate all the
\par
interventions. The EVI outcomes can also be calculated for
\par
a situation that the investigator is interested in a future
\par
comparison of a subset of treatments. Accordingly, we
\par
calculated the EVI outcomes for all possible comparisons
\par
involving two or more treatments. We drew the maximum
\par
EVPI curve as a function of WTP for QALY. We created a
\par
rank table of comparisons based on EVPIs and EVPPIs and
\par
evaluated whether the ranking of comparisons remained
\par
consistent across the PMA- and NMA-based analyses.
