\par
muscarinic agents
\par
synthesis paradigm that only incorporates direct evidence,
\par
and NMA as a paradigm that includes the entire network of
\par
evidence, on EVI outputs of a decision-analytic model. The
\par
EVI estimates for treatment effect were generally larger
\par
when evidence synthesis was carried out using a PMA of
\par
placebo-based comparisons, in contrast with the NMA of
\par
the entire network of comparisons. This makes sense, as
\par
evidence synthesis using NMA includes more RCTs and
\par
therefore is based on higher quantities of information,
\par
concordantly resulting in lower estimates of opportunity
\par
loss because of uncertainty. If such EVI outcomes are used
\par
as a figure of merit to evaluate whether conducting future
\par
studies is justifiable, it might be the case that the NMA-
\par
based analysis will recommend no need for future studies,
\par
whereas a PMA-based analysis will indicate such studies
\par
are worth conducting (or suggest studies that are already1002 Z. Zafari et al.
