Emulators are useful tools for uncertainty and sensitivity
\par
analysis [21,23]. For GP emulators in particular, this is due to the
\par
fact that Bayesian quadrature as described in [20] allows one to
\par
take advantage of the emulator's analytical properties to evaluate
\par
the expected value E{$\frac{1}{2}$}Y and the variance Var{$\frac{1}{2}$}Y relatively quickly.
\par
In particular, since Y is a GP, the integral
