3.3. Other maintenance policies
\par
In this section we have illustrated the use of emulators to
\par
perform sensitivity analysis on a maintenance optimisation pro-
\par
blem by using two standard maintenance policies, namely the age
\par
replacement policy (ARP) and the block replacement policy (BRP).
\par
In both policies, corrective repair actions restore the component to
\par
its original condition. However, as we discussed in the Introduc-
\par
tion, repair can be anything between replacement (AGAN) and
\par
minimal intervention (ABAO). To represent cases other than
\par
replacement (perfect repair), the standard ARP and BRP policies
\par
have been extended to describe minimal and imperfect repair.
\par
Within the literature one can nd reference to these wider classes
\par
of policy [5].
\par
The analysis presented here can be used for the treatment of
\par
problems with imperfect maintenance, as well. To do so, the
\par
